.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt RMXOS-OWNER-SEED 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rmxos-owner-seed
.Nd read the first owner's settings from a labelled FAT volume
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -altroot Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The base launchd job
.Pa /etc/launchd.d/org.rmxos.owner-seed.plist
runs this program once when loaded at boot.
It does nothing if an owner already exists, as defined by
.Xr rmxos-owner 8 ,
or if
.Pa /dev/msdosfs/RMXOWNER
is absent.
It does not run cloud-init or nuageinit.
.Pp
The FAT volume label is
.Cm RMXOWNER .
Its root must contain the plain regular files
.Pa hostname ,
.Pa user
and
.Pa authorized_keys .
The first two contain one value, optionally followed by a line ending;
the third contains one OpenSSH public key line.
Each file is limited to 65536 bytes.
The volume is mounted read-only at
.Pa /private/var/run/rmxos-owner-seed .
A directory there, left by a run that stopped before removing it, is
reused; anything else at that path, a symbolic link included, is refused
before the mount and nothing is written.
All files are read and validated before invoking
.Xr rmxos-owner 8
with those values and the root
.Pa / ,
so the host name and the mdo rule apply at once, without a second boot.
The volume is then unmounted and the temporary mount directory removed.
Missing or invalid input changes no owner files and produces one diagnostic
line with its reason.
Success and errors use os_log, subsystem
.Cm org.rmxos.owner-seed ,
category boot, and one line on the standard error, which the job sends to
the console for early boot visibility.
Absent volumes and existing owners are silent.
.Pp
Alternatively, enter the
.Xr rmxos-owner 8
command by hand at the console; no password is collected.
The normal mount and owner checks also apply with
.Fl -altroot .
.Sh TESTING
Host tests use the installer's RMXOS_SU_FIXTURE confinement.
Label discovery is unchanged in that mode, but the labelled provider must
be a file-backed md device below the fixture.
RMXOS_OWNER_COMMAND selects the built rmxos-owner below that fixture;
the alternate root must also lie below it.
This command override is ignored on the real system.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount_msdosfs 8 ,
.Xr rmxos-install 8 ,
.Xr rmxos-owner 8
